tasks.prompt:
A garden record stores plant details:

```
{
  "plants": [
    {"species": "rose", "height": 1.45, "watered": true},
    {"species": "fern", "height": 0.8, "watered": false}
  ]
}
```

Write a program that prints the full key path of every leaf value. For each plant print one line per field in order species, height, watered:

Line format: `plants[0].species = rose`

For Text print the value unquoted, for Real print with 1 decimal place, for Bool print `true` or `false`.

Print exactly 6 lines. No trailing spaces.

A print shop tracks ink cartridges for each press as a JSON document like {"press":"R1","inks":[{"color":"Cyan","pct":82},{"color":"Magenta","pct":45}],"jobs":6}. Below are four presses as JSON documents.

Press JSON documents:
{"press":"R1","inks":[{"color":"Cyan","pct":82},{"color":"Magenta","pct":45}],"jobs":6}
{"press":"R2","inks":[{"color":"Cyan","pct":37},{"color":"Yellow","pct":91}],"jobs":4}
{"press":"R3","inks":[{"color":"Black","pct":64},{"color":"Magenta","pct":73}],"jobs":9}
{"press":"R4","inks":[{"color":"Black","pct":22},{"color":"Yellow","pct":58}],"jobs":3}

Output one line per press in the order given, in the exact format:
PRESS <press> | INKS <count of entries in inks array> | LOWEST <smallest pct> | JOBS <jobs>
After all presses, output one line:
LOW INK COLORS <number of individual ink entries whose pct is strictly below 50>

A beekeeper records hive status as a JSON document like {"hive":"H1","queen":"seen","frames":10,"honey_kg":14.5,"mites":3}. Below are five hives as JSON documents.

Hive JSON documents:
{"hive":"H1","queen":"seen","frames":10,"honey_kg":14.5,"mites":3}
{"hive":"H2","queen":"seen","frames":12,"honey_kg":18.2,"mites":1}
{"hive":"H3","queen":"missing","frames":8,"honey_kg":9.7,"mites":6}
{"hive":"H4","queen":"seen","frames":11,"honey_kg":16.8,"mites":4}
{"hive":"H5","queen":"missing","frames":7,"honey_kg":6.3,"mites":8}

Output one line per hive in the order given, in the exact format:
HIVE <hive> | QUEEN <queen> | FRAMES <frames> | HONEY <honey_kg, one decimal place> | MITES <mites>
After all hives, output one line:
NEEDS CHECK <number of hives whose queen is missing OR whose mites are strictly greater than 5>

A marathon timing crew stores runner records as JSON documents like {"bib":"101","name":"Ana","splits":[12.5,13.1,13.4],"dnf":false}. Below are four runners as JSON documents.

Runner JSON documents:
{"bib":"101","name":"Ana","splits":[12.5,13.1,13.4],"dnf":false}
{"bib":"102","name":"Ben","splits":[11.9,12.3],"dnf":true}
{"bib":"103","name":"Cara","splits":[14.2,13.9,14.5,14.1],"dnf":false}
{"bib":"104","name":"Dev","splits":[12.8,13.0,13.2],"dnf":false}

Output one line per runner in the order given, in the exact format:
BIB <bib> | NAME <name> | SPLITS <count of entries in splits array> | TOTAL <sum of all splits, two decimal places> | DNF <dnf>
After all runners, output one line:
FASTEST AVERAGE <the runner with the smallest average split time, printed as their name>
